<Base title="About the developer"><div class="editorial-page content-width"><nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span aria-current="page">About</span></nav><p class="eyebrow">About {site.username}</p><h1>Making games<br/>out of curiosity.</h1><p class="lead">{site.introduction}</p><p class="about-ownership">{site.ownership}</p><section class="editorial-grid"><h2>Game features<br/>that work together.</h2><div><p>Changing gravity affects both movement and animation. Rewinding a character means recording where it has been. Shared objects need clear rules across players.</p><p>I also build the everyday features around those mechanics: rewards after a round, cosmetics in a shop, and saved progress. You can explore the gameplay first and ask me about the implementation in a project enquiry.</p><a class="text-link" href="/#projects">Explore the projects ↗</a></div></section><section class="editorial-grid"><h2>Independent work.<br/>Clear attribution.</h2><div><p>{site.responsibilityNote}</p><p>The project descriptions are based on reviews of their code. Each project separates implemented features from behavior that still needs a current gameplay recording, and identifies important limitations.</p><p>Gravity Dash’s surface-normal sampling is credited to EmilyBendsSpace’s DevForum example. The project’s showcase is the adapted controller’s integration and the surrounding spatial systems.</p></div></section><section class="editorial-grid"><h2>For your project</h2><div><p>I can help build gameplay features, investigate bugs, improve multiplayer interactions, and review how a game manages saved data.</p><a class="button button-primary" href="/services/">See the work I can help with ↗</a></div></section></div></Base>

